// @entry SYN-STRUCT
// @desc Human synth-program structure prior art: a synth is organized as
// @desc small helper functions (oscillator, envelope, clamp, floor) plus one
// @desc render function per voice/vector that fills a byte buffer with
// @desc little-endian 16-bit samples, plus a main that (1) reads argv[1] as
// @desc the output path and argv[2] as the vector selector, (2) allocates
// @desc the sample buffer, (3) dispatches to the selected render function,
// @desc (4) opens the output file with open(2), writes the 44-byte WAV
// @desc header then the samples, and closes. No globals, no RNG, all sizes
// @desc from the vector parameters.
// @desc Structure template (vector parameters filled from the task spec):
// @desc   helpers: synth_floor, synth_sin, synth_phase, synth_adsr, synth_clamp
// @desc   render_vN(b:[]u8): fills b with 2*count little-endian bytes
// @desc   main: argv parse -> buffer alloc -> render dispatch ->
// @desc         open/write header/write samples/close via raw syscalls
